# TypeScript Conventions

## Imports

Barrel imports only — always import from folder index, not from individual files:

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
import { logError, notifyAdmins } from '../lib';
import { WarrantyService } from '../services';

// ❌ BAD
import { logError } from '../lib/logError';
```

## Error handling

Always log and notify admins on errors:

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
try {
  await WarrantyService.create(...);
} catch (err) {
  logError(err, 'createWarranty');
  await notifyAdmins(`❌ Ошибка создания гарантии: ${String(err)}`);
}

// ❌ BAD — silent catch
try { ... } catch {}
```

## Env variables

Always import from `config/variables.ts`, never read `process.env` directly in feature code.

## Services

Business logic lives in `services/`. Commands only call services and send replies — no DB queries in command handlers.

## Text content

All user-facing HTML strings go in `text/index.ts`. No inline HTML in commands.

## Strict mode

`strict: true` is enforced. No `any`, no non-null assertions unless genuinely necessary.
